    "content": "Federal income taxes for the 2025 tax year are due on Wednesday, April 15, 2026. Taxpayers must file their returns or request an extension by this date to avoid penalties, and payment for any taxes owed is due by April 15, regardless of extension requests.Key 2026 tax deadlines include:April 15, 2026: Deadline to file 2025 tax returns, pay taxes owed, and file for a 6-month extension.October 15, 2026: Final deadline for those who requested an automatic extension.Estimated Tax Payments: Quarterly payments for 2026 are due April 15, June 15, September 15, and January 15 (2027).Important Information:IRS Free File: The IRS Free File program began accepting returns on Jan. 9, 2026, with the full season opening on Jan. 26.Extensions: Filing an extension on or before April 15 gives you until Oct. 15 to submit paperwork, but it does not extend the time to pay any taxes owed.State Taxes: Many states align with the federal deadline, but some vary (e.g., Louisiana deadline is May 15).Special Circumstances: Select counties in Tennessee affected by storms have an extended deadline of May 22, 2026.For further guidance, consult the Guide to filing your taxes in 2026 from the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau.",
